            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>DIALOG_TELEPORTMAN_DEFEATED</LocID>                                  <Text>{LOC:UNIT_NEUTRAL_TELEPORTMAN} sconfitta</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>DIALOG_TELEPORTMAN_DEFEATED_TEXT</LocID>                             <Text>{LOC:UNIT_NEUTRAL_TELEPORTMAN} conferisce all'eroe vittorioso la capacità di teletrasportarsi in qualsiasi luogo della mappa già visitato in precedenza.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>DIALOG_SELECT_TARGET</LocID>                                         <Text>Seleziona la destinazione del teletrasporto</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ARTIFACT_BIOTIC_MENTOR</LocID>                                       <Text>Biotic Mentor</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ARTIFACT_BIOTIC_MENTOR_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                           <Text>Allows your commander to use BIO abilities twice per round.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ARTIFACT_BIOTIC_MENTOR_LORE</LocID>                                  <Text>"Though my mind is still untouched by the artifact, I have experienced hair loss, finger elongation, and the rash became so itchy ... I scratched the skin off ... and uncovered at least a dozen new eyes underneath ... I named some of them: Blinky, Winky, and Soulpiercer!"  </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ARTIFACT_PSYKER_GENIE</LocID>                                        <Text>Genie</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ARTIFACT_PSYKER_GENIE_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                            <Text>Your PSY abilities last twice as long!</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ARTIFACT_PSYKER_GENIE_LORE</LocID>                                   <Text>"I know you, stupid! You would totally mess up those three wishes! So I will grant you only one and choose it for you. I will make you a psyker so powerful that no lunatic asylum will be able to hold you, and no psychiatrist will be able to repair you."  </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_TRIFFID_ROOT</LocID>                                       <Text>Triffid Root</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_TRIFFID_ROOT_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                           <Text>The commander gains 10 new Triffid units for their army each cycle!</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_TRIFFID_ROOT_LORE</LocID>                                  <Text>Or you can put it in a press and get the most exquisite, delicious juice in the world! The burden of choice. I feel you, bro. </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_TAX_COLLECTORS_BANNER</LocID>                              <Text>Tax Collector's Banner</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_TAX_COLLECTORS_BANNER_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                  <Text><![CDATA[The commander gains <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>1000 Aura Coins</color> when taking over buildings on the map.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_TAX_COLLECTORS_BANNER_LORE</LocID>                         <Text>Join the Leaches Club! Enjoy the company of such legends as public transport inspectors, company owners, and landlords ... Wait a minute! I must have been infected by some virulent form of ideology! I hope it's treatable! ... By medicine provided by the state healthcare system! ... For free!   </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_PATHFINDER</LocID>                                         <Text>Pathfinder Drone</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_PATHFINDER_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                             <Text>Removes movement penalties for rough terrain.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_PATHFINDER_LORE</LocID>                                    <Text>No more blue-on-blue roadkills during marches through difficult terrain. Did I say roadkill? I meant, your husband died a hero's death ... in combat!</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_UNIVERSAL_JAMMER</LocID>                                   <Text>Expropriator</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_UNIVERSAL_JAMMER_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                       <Text>Turrets and outposts defeated by this commander don't get destroyed, but are taken over. </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_UNIVERSAL_JAMMER_LORE</LocID>                              <Text>What was briefly yours, is now mine. In the world of ones and zeroes, it's as easy as that.   </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>NEUTRAL_ARMY_EXTRA_UNITS_FROM_EQUIPMENT</LocID>                      <Text>Thanks to your equipment, some units would like to join your army if you make space for them!</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_STIM_TAC</LocID>                                          <Text>Stim-tac</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_STIM_TAC_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                              <Text><![CDATA[Increases <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>Combat power by +5</color> for three phases.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_STIM_TAC_LORE</LocID>                                     <Text>All peak performance athletes and your favorite movie stars take it, so why are you still small and weak, you pathetic piece of ... !!! Erm, what I am trying to say is, girls will love the new "you"!  </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>STATUS_EFFECT_STIM_TAC</LocID>                                       <Text><![CDATA[Stim-tac used: <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>combat power +5</color>]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_TUMORI_POTION</LocID>                                     <Text>Potion of Motion</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_TUMORI_POTION_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                         <Text><![CDATA[Increases <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>Exploration proficiency by +5</color> for three phases.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_TUMORI_POTION_LORE</LocID>                                <Text>I will not go into details of the manufacturing process, but given that you are already accustomed to drinking the secretion of metamorphosed sweat glands, better known as "milk", you'll be just fine drinking this. </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>STATUS_EFFECT_TUMORI_POTION</LocID>                                  <Text><![CDATA[Potion of Motion used: <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>exploration proficiency +5</color>]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_BRAIN_STIM</LocID>                                        <Text>Brain fuel</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_BRAIN_STIM_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                            <Text><![CDATA[Increases <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>Ability power by +5</color> for three phases.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_BRAIN_STIM_LORE</LocID>                                   <Text>It was a placebo, my friend. You were that smart all along! The secret ingredient was self-confidence! ... with a pinch of LSD.  </Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>STATUS_EFFECT_BRAIN_STIM</LocID>                                     <Text><![CDATA[Brain fuel used: <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>ability power +5</color>]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_BURN_PUNCHER_DESCRIPTION_V2</LocID>                        <Text><![CDATA[Melee attacks inflict Burning to BIO units and Corrosion to TECH units]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_PIERCING_AMMO</LocID>                                      <Text>Piercing ammo</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_PIERCING_AMMO_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                          <Text>Ranged units always deal critical damage.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EQUIPMENT_PIERCING_AMMO_LORE</LocID>                                 <Text>Turn your enemy's bulletproof vest into dead weight!</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>


            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>SKILL_EFFECT_MOVEMENT_PERCENT_REFILLED_AFTER_VICTORY</LocID>         <Text><![CDATA[Victory in battle restores {1}% <color=SOTS_COLOR_MOVEMENT>Movement Points</color>.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>SKILL_EFFECT_ENERGY_PERCENT_REFILLED_AFTER_VICTORY</LocID>           <Text><![CDATA[Victory in battle restores {1}% <color=SOTS_COLOR_ENERGY>Energy Points</color>.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>HERO_SKILL_SCAVENGER_DESCRIPTION_V2</LocID>                          <Text><![CDATA[Consente al comandante di <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>recuperare parte dei materiali</color> con cui era composto un esercito sconfitto e di <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>raccogliere ulteriori risorse</color> sulla mappa.]]></Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>SKILL_EFFECT_COLLECT_EXTRA_RESOURCES</LocID>                         <Text><![CDATA[La quantità di risorse gratuite raccolte sulla mappa viene <color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>aumentata del {1}%</color> (o almeno di 1).]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>STATUS_EFFECT_PURSUED</LocID>                                        <Text><![CDATA[<color=SOTS_COLOR_RED>Pursued/tracked.</color> -20 to morale and -2 to unit initiative]]></Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EFFECT_WHILE_IN_RANGE</LocID>                                        <Text>Active while in the range of the source.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>            
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAPOBJ_OUTPOST_TURRET_UPGRADE</LocID>                                <Text>Aggiungi una torretta difensiva.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAPOBJ_OUTPOST_UPG_TURRET_UPGRADE</LocID>                            <Text>Aggiungi una grande torretta difensiva.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>            
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>DIALOG_EVACUATION_ABILITY_TEXT_V2</LocID>                            <Text>Choose a nearby base to evacuate to!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EVACUATION_TOO_FAR</LocID>                                           <Text>Too far</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EVACUATION_DISTANCE</LocID>                                          <Text>Distance</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_EXPLORATION_EVACUATION_DESCRIPTION_V2</LocID>           <Text>Teletrasporta il comandante e il suo esercito in una base a scelta. La portata dipende dal livello dell'abilità; la base più vicina è sempre disponibile.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_EXPLORATION_EVACUATION_DESCRIPTION_LVL1</LocID>         <Text>Distanza fino a 20 caselle.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_EXPLORATION_EVACUATION_DESCRIPTION_LVL2</LocID>         <Text>Distanza fino a 30 caselle.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_EXPLORATION_EVACUATION_DESCRIPTION_LVL3</LocID>         <Text>Distanza fino a 40 caselle.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_NEUTRAL_CREATURE</LocID>                                <Text>Evoca creatura</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_NEUTRAL_CREATURE_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                    <Text>Evoca un'unità neutrale casuale in una posizione scelta</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_NEUTRAL_CREATURE_DESCRIPTION_LVL1</LocID>               <Text>Livello creatura 1-3</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_NEUTRAL_CREATURE_DESCRIPTION_LVL2</LocID>               <Text>Livello creatura 3-5</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_NEUTRAL_CREATURE_DESCRIPTION_LVL3</LocID>               <Text>Livello creatura 5-7</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <!--New Units-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_CRABORG</LocID>                                         <Text>Granchio-cyborg</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_CRABORG_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                             <Text>Il loro metabolismo accelerato comporta non solo riflessi rapidi, ma anche una riproduzione veloce. Talmente veloce, infatti, che i conigli australiani sembrano quasi frigidi al confronto. È chiaro come il sole: li hanno creati i Fossoriani! I loro impianti, i loro marchi da laboratorio, il loro... TUTTO! Ma quei bastardi pelosi continuano a negare ogni accusa e non si assumono alcuna responsabilità!</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_CRABORG_PASSIVE_INFO_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                <Text>Quando più della metà del gruppo viene eliminato, i Granchio-cyborg si infuriano. Ottengono un attacco doppio, ma il loro comandante perde il controllo su di loro.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_TELEPORTMAN</LocID>                                     <Text>Camminatore del Vuoto</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_TELEPORTMAN_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                         <Text>Ci sono voluti mesi, un’enorme quantità di impegno e risorse, ma abbiamo scoperto… in realtà, niente! Non riusciamo a catturarli… è proprio così semplice. Sì, sì, sono di origine Primordiale, possono teletrasportarsi e, se uccisi, lasciano uno strappo spazio-temporale temporaneo. Questo è tutto, gente, andate a casa.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_TELEPORTMAN_PASSIVE_INFO_DESCRIPTION</LocID>            <Text>Può attaccare qualsiasi unità sul campo di battaglia.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_HEDGEHOG</LocID>                                        <Text>Riccio</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_HEDGEHOG_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                            <Text>Perché riccio? Perché le lame sono rinforzate con una struttura cristallina che conferisce loro le proprietà di una lama d’acciaio, e non mi riferisco all’acciaio delle officine pakistane, ma a quello delle katana di Hattori Hanzo.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>UNIT_NEUTRAL_HEDGEHOG_PASSIVE_INFO_DESCRIPTION</LocID>               <Text>Contrattacchi illimitati che infliggono danni da veleno, corrosivi e da emorragia.</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>

            <!--SF Campaign ship - Chiquita -->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAPOBJ_PIRATESSHUTTLE</LocID>                                        <Text>Astronave della Flotta Sovrana</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAPOBJ_PIRATESSHUTTLE_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                            <Text>Il tipo preferito dai contrabbandieri e dai commercianti senza scrupoli. </Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAPOBJ_CAMPAIGN_PIRATESSHUTTLE</LocID>                               <Text>Piccolino</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAPOBJ_CAMPAIGN_PIRATESSHUTTLE_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                   <Text>L’astronave più veloce della Flotta Sovrana.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_COMBAT_ENERGY_DRAIN_DESCRIPTION_V2</LocID>              <Text><![CDATA[Steal half the <color=SOTS_COLOR_ENERGY>energy</color> of the enemy commander.]]></Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <!--Redesign-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>ABILITY_HERO_EXPLORATION_PROTECTIVE_FIELD_DESCRIPTION_V2</LocID>     <Text>Crea un campo protettivo che impedisce agli oggetti, alle abilità e ai vari pericoli incontrati di infliggere effetti negativi.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_MAGNESIUM_TORCH_DESCRIPTION_V4</LocID>                    <Text><![CDATA[<color=SOTS_COLOR_GOLD>Reveals a large area in the Nebbia di guerra</color> around a chosen position within the commander's own visibility range.]]></Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CONSUMABLE_NOT_INSIDE_A_BASE</LocID>                                 <Text><![CDATA[<color=SOTS_COLOR_RED>Can't be used inside a base.</color>]]></Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>

            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MAP_SPECIFICATIONS_MAP_LOCK_STARTING_ARMIES</LocID>                  <Text>Lock starting armies</Text></GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <!--_______________NEUTRAL ZONE__________________________-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>        <LocID>NEUTRAL_ZONE_ID</LocID>                                               <Text>Zona neutrale</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>        <LocID>NEUTRAL_ZONE_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                                      <Text>What if all armies in the region only consisted of neutral creatures?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>        <LocID>NEUTRAL_ZONE_INTRO</LocID>                                            <Text>Somewhere on the outskirts of the Siren System ...</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>        <LocID>NEUTRAL_ZONE_VICTORY</LocID>                                          <Text>Neutral zone no longer exists; the Fossorians have expanded their sphere of influence once again! Glory to the Supreme Leader! </Text>    </GameDBLocalizedString>


            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_01</LocID>                                <Text>Supreme Leader, we've landed! \nBut, we have many questions: where are we? Why are we here exactly? Why couldn't we travel on our own ship? And above all, why bring all these pseudo-units instead of our own soldiers?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SUPREME_01</LocID>                              <Text>The exact coordinates are not important, Agent. You are going undercover, that's why the ship and the army.\nBelow you lies a territory controlled by the so-called Neutral Pacifist Union, grass-eaters who do not recognize the official faction armies. The entire region is rich in Aura coin production – and we want it for ourselves.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_02</LocID>                                <Text>Ah, I see, but with this army we won't take anything!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SUPREME_02</LocID>                              <Text>That's only plan B. Plan A is for you to disguise yourself as the All-Mother and try to convince them to give up the territory. Molly and Hak are your backup.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_03</LocID>                                <Text>I see. I figured that the costume we carried on the ship wasn't just for fighting off the general gloominess.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_04</LocID>                                <Text>I'm ready, just please wash the costume next time, it smells like a possum died in it.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_05</LocID>                                <Text>I really have a bad feeling about this, being stuck in this costume, and my ass is sore from that hover device that's supposed to make me look like I'm levitating ... Wait, someone's coming!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_CLOKI_01</LocID>                                <Text>OOOOH MIGHTY AND ALL-GLORIOUS!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_ADELA_01</LocID>                                <Text>We welcome you among us, most exalted one!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SANTARSI_01</LocID>                             <Text>.,.,.,....,---- blessed one----..,.,...--,</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_WINKY_01</LocID>                                <Text>What brings you to us? \n... and why did you arrive on that godforsaken Sovereign ship?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_06</LocID>                                <Text>Damn, what am I supposed to tell them?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SUPREME_03</LocID>                              <Text>Improvise, you fool!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_RELIC_01</LocID>                                <Text>Hear me, hear me… I, the great OLD-MOTHER, hereby ...</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SUPREME_04</LocID>                              <Text>ALL-MOTHER, you idiot!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_RELIC_02</LocID>                                <Text>I mean ... I, the Great ALL-MOTHER, hereby command you ...</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_CLOKI_02</LocID>                                <Text>Wait, wait, what are you trying to say?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_ADELA_02</LocID>                                <Text>Yeah, and what's that buzzing sound coming from ... your ass?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_WINKY_02</LocID>                                <Text>Also, why do you smell like a dead possum? </Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SANTARSI_02</LocID>                             <Text>.,.,.,....,---- false ALL-MOTHER---..,.,...--</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_CLOKI_03</LocID>                                <Text>Adela to the UNSS ship "Spring Breeze"! Immediately target that little red ship parked on an asteroid in orbit!\n... can't you hear me?! Now!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_RAK_01</LocID>                                  <Text>Damn it!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_ADELA_03</LocID>                                <Text>You've screwed up, Fossorian. You're not the first one who tried to scam us. Now you're going to starve to death here. You're only lucky we're such sunshine-loving pacifists and don't believe in physical punishment. \nCome on, let's get out of here!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_07</LocID>                                <Text>So, that went well ... but at least I can take this stinking disguise off! What now?</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_SUPREME_05</LocID>                              <Text>Plan B! I'll send somebody to pick you up once you've taken care of those dung-eaters.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_AGENT_08</LocID>                                <Text>Well ... what a cunning plan that was! \nAnyway, let's do this the old-fashioned way. Molly, Hak! Party time!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>OBJECTIVE_NEUTRAL_ZONE_01</LocID>                                    <Text>Defeat all enemies!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>

        </LocalizedStrings>
    </GameDBStringTable>
